/* book exam traps: HETP is height per ideal stage; HTU is height per transfer unit. They are not interchangeable. | In the NTU integral, divide by y − y*, the local overall driving force, not by y alone, and integrate from the outlet y2 up to the inlet y1. | Kya is volumetric, per m³ of packed volume. Ky without a is per m² of interface and cannot be used directly in HTU = G/(Kya). | Stage efficiency is E = Nideal/Nactual. Actual trays = ideal/E, so E below 1 always raises the tray count. | The terminal compositions in NTU are gas mole fractions yin and yout, not tray numbers or liquid compositions. */
